# Copy to `.env` at the repository root and fill in. That file is gitignored.
#
#   cp .env.example .env && chmod 600 .env
#   python -m qbs.agent --check
#
# `qbs.agent` reads this file on import, so the CLI, the dashboard and a
# notebook all pick it up with nothing further to do.
#
# A real environment variable ALWAYS wins over a line here, so
# `GOOGLE_API_KEY=... python -m qbs.agent ...` overrides the file for one run.
#
# Syntax is deliberately small: KEY=value, one per line, `#` starts a comment
# only at the beginning of a line, and a matching pair of surrounding quotes
# is stripped. No `$VAR` interpolation and no multi-line values -- export
# those from your shell instead.

# --- required for the LLM analyst ----------------------------------------
# https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# GEMINI_API_KEY is accepted too; Google's own docs use both names.
GOOGLE_API_KEY=

# --- optional -------------------------------------------------------------
# Which Gemini model the analyst uses. Model names move faster than this repo,
# so this is the dial to turn when a default stops resolving. Flash is the
# cheaper, faster option.
# QBS_GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash

# Better web search than the keyless DuckDuckGo default, and it costs money.
# Set this AND `pip install tavily-python`; qbs.agent.news then prefers it.
# TAVILY_API_KEY=

# Nothing else in this package needs a key. Prices come from Yahoo via
# yfinance, and the Interactive Brokers credentials for live trading live in
# deploy/docker/.env instead -- a different file, on the trading host only.
